<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:47:56 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>🔴Live: Israeli exit polls show narrow edge for opposition but no clear majority against Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-live-polls-open-in-first-israeli-election-since-october-7-attack</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">178d1448-d243-11f1-bc11-55c39fb7a334</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:16:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Netanyahu govt has 'attacked' Israeli judicial system, Supreme Court and democratic institutions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-govt-has-attacked-israeli-judicial-system-supreme-court-and-democratic-institutions</link><description>
Annette Young is pleased to welcome Alain Greilsammer, Professor of Political Science at Bar-Ilan University in Tel Aviv. In the wake of the October 7 attacks, regional tensions with Iran, and deepening domestic divisions, Greilsammer argues that the election will be fundamentally shaped by concerns over democratic accountability, judicial independence and the unequal distribution of civic obligations. He warns Netanyahu’s policies risk transforming Israel into “something like an authoritarian or non-democratic state.” He suggests that Israel’s Arab political parties could play a decisive role in determining the election’s outcome. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/44b94f32-d215-11f1-870d-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-130828-131530-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/44b94f32-d215-11f1-870d-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-130828-131530-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4a9e2b0c-d215-11f1-bbd3-8db6a196f0d8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:44:07 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ibrahim Abu Ahmad on Israeli election: 'Crucial for Arab citizens to have ally in Jewish community'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-ibrahim-abu-ahmad-on-israeli-election-crucial-for-arab-citizens-to-have-ally-in-jewish-community</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Ibrahim Abu Ahmad, Author, Palestinian Israeli political and peace activist and Head of Social Media for Israel's left-wing Democrats. “Currently, the sentiment in Israel is built around fear and trauma,” explains Ahmad. His most striking observation concerns the apparent contradiction between political leadership and public sentiment: “Many want to see an Arab-Jewish coalition. It's the leadership that is afraid to say it.” Ultimately, he moves beyond conventional electoral calculations to frame Arab-Jewish partnership as a question of democratic survival.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b957c3a8-d235-11f1-be1e-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-160657-162025-CS-01.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b957c3a8-d235-11f1-be1e-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-160657-162025-CS-01.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bf66238e-d235-11f1-a9a7-358d90d616ad</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:59:43 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>How student assemblies brought down the Serbian government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261027-how-student-assemblies-brought-down-the-serbian-government</link><description>
A list of academics, engineers, artists and activists chosen by Serbia’s student assemblies defeated long-ruling president Aleksandar Vucic's right-wing Serbian Progressive Party Sunday. The shock victory comes after nearly two years of student-led anti-corruption protests – and may serve as a model for other movements hoping to turn street demonstrations into concrete political change.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4370c334-d225-11f1-9cd7-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T200342Z-473553852-RC26BOAEJNFQ-RTRMADP-3-SERBIA-ELECTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4370c334-d225-11f1-9cd7-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T200342Z-473553852-RC26BOAEJNFQ-RTRMADP-3-SERBIA-ELECTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">58ef0ee2-d224-11f1-aae6-b7e084e46075</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:58:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4370c334-d225-11f1-9cd7-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-26T200342Z-473553852-RC26BOAEJNFQ-RTRMADP-3-SERBIA-ELECTION.jpg">© Marko Djurica, Reuters</source><dc:creator>Paul MILLAR</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli elections a 'referendum' on Netanyahu, security and whether Israel will 'remain a democracy'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-elections-a-referendum-on-netanyahu-security-and-whether-israel-will-remain-a-democracy</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Ron Gerlitz, CEO of aChord Center at Hebrew University, an Israeli organization specialising in the social psychology of intergroup relations. “The main issue in this election is the fight for Israeli democracy,” explains Gerlitz. And beneath the struggle over democratic institutions lies the erosion of Benjamin Netanyahu's longstanding association with national security. Gerlitz also examines the psychological foundations of Netanyahu's enduring support, the influence of conspiracy narratives, the electoral significance of Arab parties and the uncertain future of the two-state solution.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/029a5de6-d227-11f1-88b5-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-151044-152521-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/029a5de6-d227-11f1-88b5-47de50b3c1e4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-151044-152521-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08356f48-d227-11f1-b360-5985141447d7</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:34:19 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴Live: Israeli election committee refuses Netanyahu's request to extend voting hours</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-live-polls-open-in-first-israeli-election-since-october-7-attack</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">87908aa4-d234-11f1-8bc9-e1bfc51244ba</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:30:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Rights groups say proposed French law to make rioters pay for damage is anti-democratic</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261027-rights-groups-say-proposed-french-law-to-make-rioters-pay-for-damage-anti-democratic</link><description>
Critics have said that a proposed French law that would make rioters liable to pay thousands of euros for any damage they cause is anti-democratic, as it could undermine the legitimate right to protest. The government put forward the law in a bid to quell looting and vandalism on the fringes of ongoing national protests over poor conditions in French schools and the high cost of living.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49db0b42-d231-11f1-9ade-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294363892004.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49db0b42-d231-11f1-9ade-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294363892004.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4fb3f650-d231-11f1-ab55-d72d8aeb94ab</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:27:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49db0b42-d231-11f1-9ade-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26294363892004.jpg">© Teresa Suarez, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Lawmakers hold a minute of silence for Pengo Bossio Wangi, victim of racist attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-france-lawmakers-hold-a-minute-of-silence-for-pengo-bossio-wangi-victim-of-racist-attack-1</link><description>
French lawmakers held a minute of silence for Pengo Bossio Wangi. The victim of a racist attack died in a shooting last week, while at least five other people were wounded, including a 12-years-old girl. FRANCE 24’s Claire Paccalin reports from the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d26e3818-d226-11f1-a4c7-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3b57773c.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d26e3818-d226-11f1-a4c7-a7bbbeea0b20/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-3b57773c.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fa737d4c-d225-11f1-888e-9500dea4febf</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 17:08:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israelis vote in a tense election: What's at stake?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israelis-vote-in-a-tense-election-what-s-at-stake</link><description>
Israelis were voting Tuesday (October 27) in a tense national election widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership since the Hamas-led Oct. 7, 2023, attack on Israel and the wars that have since shaken the Middle East.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e9752f2-d226-11f1-b354-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-163137-163342-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6e9752f2-d226-11f1-b354-bf69a9ce9852/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-163137-163342-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">745b18ea-d226-11f1-8986-e734320f3c2e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:59:06 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel elections: voter turnout reaches 55% by 4pm local time</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-elections-voter-turnout-reaches-55-by-4pm-local-time</link><description>
Israelis flocked to the polls Tuesday (October 27) in turnout unseen in decades, with a deeply divided electorate delivering a verdict on veteran right-wing Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu in the first election since the October 7, 2023 attack. FRANCE24's Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6478d3e-d226-11f1-8753-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7dc5f0be.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f6478d3e-d226-11f1-8753-efcc5769f1db/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7dc5f0be.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e7f5f6cc-d225-11f1-9ba7-a50718b24c28</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:52:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil's defeated candidate Flavio Bolsonaro heads to US despite cancelled passports</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261027-defeated-brazilian-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro-passports-cancelled-whereabouts-unknown</link><description>
Brazil's former presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro fled to the US, sources said Tuesday, despite his passports being cancelled after he failed to comply with a Supreme Court order to hand them over as part of a money laundering probe. Bolsonaro's whereabouts had been a source of speculation since his election defeat on Sunday to leftist incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a7c52da-d221-11f1-9049-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299067954788.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a7c52da-d221-11f1-9049-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299067954788.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">95b0224c-d221-11f1-864e-f1256c5a284c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:33:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a7c52da-d221-11f1-9049-75c7729144f1/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299067954788.jpg">© Eraldo Peres, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>USA: Could a Democrat win a statewide election in Texas?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-usa-could-a-democrat-win-a-statewide-election-in-texas</link><description>
There is only one week left until the US midterm elections. In Texas, Democratic candidate James Talarico, could win a Senate seat for the first time in decades.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c073ffe-d215-11f1-91ad-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299284061928.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1c073ffe-d215-11f1-91ad-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26299284061928.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">71ea8724-d214-11f1-a70b-95616215da57</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:47:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Africa's Ebola outbreak tops 10,000 cases, mainly in DR Congo</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20261027-africa-ebola-outbreak-tops-10-000-cases-mainly-dr-congo</link><description>
Africa's outbreak of the Ebola virus has passed more than 10,000 cases, health authorities said Tuesday, with the vast majority located in Democratic Republic of Congo. There are currently no approved vaccines for the rare Bundibugyo species of Ebola driving the current infections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f829b28-d219-11f1-aa6f-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26269826068205.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f829b28-d219-11f1-aa6f-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26269826068205.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ea553966-d219-11f1-a266-f94f8c9bba93</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:45:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8f829b28-d219-11f1-aa6f-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26269826068205.jpg">© Sebastien Kitsa Musayi, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴Live: Netanyahu's party asks to extend Israeli election hours amid record turnout</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-live-polls-open-in-first-israeli-election-since-october-7-attack</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">744c4c66-d21c-11f1-9194-2f4d234ed90c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:39:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel votes in decisive election: What happens after polls close?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-israel-s-unique-political-system-what-happens-after-polls-close</link><description>
Israelis are voting in a pivotal election Tuesday (October 27) as their country wrestles with unresolved wars, continues to reel from Hamas' 2023 attack and is deeply divided over the character of the state and the right person to lead it. Details by FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor, Angela Diffley.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/26988dbe-d216-11f1-add4-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9b7810f8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/26988dbe-d216-11f1-add4-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9b7810f8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e2ccdb20-d211-11f1-a5c3-171811636c23</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:55:49 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>arts24</category><title>Canadian dance-punk legend Peaches reaches the ripe age of 60</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261027-canadian-dance-punk-legend-peaches-reaches-the-ripe-age-of-60</link><description>
Canadian electroclash artist Peaches has been delighting, amusing and shocking music lovers and festivalgoers for the past three decades. Her shows are also a safe space for all genders and sexualities, although less so if you are averse to crowd surfing, extravagant pubic wigs and body-augmenting costumes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53e5ebdc-d210-11f1-b848-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-74316f00.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/53e5ebdc-d210-11f1-b848-4d317af013fd/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-74316f00.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0649be20-d211-11f1-a116-1d34a11c9cc4</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:50:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marjorie HACHE</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Turnout high as Israeli voters deliver verdict on Netanyahu</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/turnout-high-as-israeli-voters-deliver-verdict-on-netanyahu</link><description>
Israelis flocked to the polls Tuesday (October 27) in turnout unseen in decades, with a deeply divided electorate delivering a verdict on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu in the first election since the October 7, 2023 attack. Former FRANCE 24 correspondent, Irris Makler, tells us more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95a21d00-d212-11f1-a0b4-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-150546-151042-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/95a21d00-d212-11f1-a0b4-5b4a75578ebb/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261027-150546-151042-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9aac309c-d212-11f1-ae4b-112991d1df27</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:45:08 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel: Netanyahu supporters gather as PM votes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-netanyahu-supporters-gather-as-pm-votes</link><description>
Supporters of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu gathered outside a polling station where the leader was voting on Tuesday. This is Israel's first election since the October7, 2023 Hamas attack and is seen as a referendum on Netanyahu. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali reports from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a29a441e-d213-11f1-b65d-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/cover-174.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a29a441e-d213-11f1-b65d-bba4eee3dc72/w:1024/p:16x9/cover-174.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f53db742-d212-11f1-8496-c5c7d9541c07</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:37:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>As China's Communist Party holds plenum, Xi's anti-corruption drive continues</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/perspective/20261027-as-china-s-communist-party-holds-plenum-xi-s-anti-corruption-drive-continues</link><description>
In this edition of Perspective, we try to figure out what happens behind the closed doors of the Chinese Communist Party's plenum meeting. At the heart of the discussions will be President Xi Jinping's firm grip on power. For analysis, we're joined by Jean-François Di Méglio from the Asia Centre think tank.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb005232-d20f-11f1-b098-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-44ed4aec.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fb005232-d20f-11f1-b098-bdb9616e85cf/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-44ed4aec.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b72c6f3c-d1f6-11f1-bb99-439aefe66b67</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:16:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charles PELLEGRIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France's Senate takes on the 'rioters pay' bill after protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261027-france-s-senate-takes-on-the-rioters-pay-bill-after-protests</link><description>
If the French Senate passes this bill, rioters will have to pay for the damage caused during the recent unrest across the country. This "casseurs-payeurs" bill comes in the wake of nationwide violence. This draft law now has an explosive add-on aimed at social media. Senators will vote on whether the government can block platforms that are too slow to act on authorities' reports of dangerous content. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e52261dc-d1fe-11f1-b43c-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1c3031f6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e52261dc-d1fe-11f1-b43c-4b25c96ec90e/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1c3031f6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8b96ed1e-d1fd-11f1-b4b7-85fc3689f01c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:13:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Entre Nous</category><title>Revisiting the delicate art of French patisserie</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261027-revisiting-the-delicate-art-of-french-patisserie</link><description>
In this edition of Entre Nous, we meet Nour Kandler, a self-taught pastry chef whose approach to French patisserie is shaped by a deep appreciation for its traditions and the rich flavours of her Middle Eastern heritage. She shares her unique perspective on pastry, where classic French techniques intertwine with cultural influences to create a style that is both personal and distinctive.
